{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they quarreled.</b> It says \"the people\" and not \"all the people,\" as it says concerning the manna, for there were two groups: one that had no water to drink, and it is the one that makes a quarrel with Moses, and the second that has water which they brought from Alush, and it is the one that wishes to test HaShem, whether He will give water, as I shall explain:" "<b>Give us water.</b> They are speaking to Moses and Aaron, and there is no need to mention Aaron, for I have already explained that Moses did not speak with Israel except through Aaron. And behold, he answered those who quarreled with him: \"Why do you quarrel with me? Let us all cry out to HaShem,\" and he said to those who test: \"Why do you test YHWH?\""], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:16.899112701Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}